<h2 class="font-headline text-3xl font-bold text-primary mb-8">A simpler way to clear space</h2>
<div class="space-y-5 text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
<p>Canyon Coast is a fictional junk-removal company created to demonstrate a polished local-service website. The brand is not presented as an active contractor or a real operating business.</p>
<p>The customer promise is intentionally simple: describe the job, share a few photos, receive a clear estimate, and choose a convenient pickup window.</p>
<p>The sample pricing and service descriptions show how a real company could explain its process without making customers hunt for the basics.</p>
<h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mt-8 mb-3">What we do</h3>
<p>Residential and commercial junk removal: garage cleanouts, estate cleanouts, appliance haul, e-waste, office de-commissioning, storage unit turnovers, tenant turnouts. Light demolition: sheds, decks, fences, hot tubs, interior walls, concrete slab breakout on smaller jobs. One crew, one truck, tear-out and haul-away in the same visit.</p>
<h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mt-8 mb-3">How we work</h3>
<p>Customers send photos, a ZIP code, and timing details so the crew can estimate the load before scheduling. Larger or unusually complex jobs may need an on-site review.</p>
<p>Before launch, the final operator would replace these sample promises with its real response times, policies, insurance information, and service capacity.</p>
<h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mt-8 mb-3">Where your stuff actually ends up</h3>
<p>We sort every load before it hits the dump. Metal goes to the scrap yard. Electronics go to certified e-waste recyclers. Working appliances, reusable furniture, and unopened household goods get routed to local donation partners when there's a fit. It's more work than backing up to the dump and dropping everything, and it's the only reason we can call this an eco-friendly operation honestly.</p>
<h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mt-8 mb-3">Credentials</h3>
<p>License, insurance, and certificate-of-insurance language is intentionally withheld until a real operator supplies verified details.</p>
<h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mt-8 mb-3">Where we work</h3>
<p>The demo is written for San Diego County, including San Diego, Poway, Escondido, and Rancho Bernardo. A real operator should confirm the final service radius before publishing.</p>
